  "body": "## What we found\n\nThe work on issue 1715 (split of the `shared_face_bodies` 3D Finish test) found this. The test job has two operations: the 3D Pocket `R1` and the 3D Finish `S1`. The test generates `S1` only. `R1` stays at status `never`.\n\nThus the verify gate does not run. The `verify` reply has:\n\n```\n\"gate\":{\"ok\":false,\"problems\":[],\"skipped\":\"an operation is stale or never generated - regenerate before judging the program\"}\n```\n\nThe test asserts that no entry of `gate.problems` starts with `gouge`. The list is always empty, so the assert checks nothing. This was true for the old whole-span test `the_sample_as_imported_still_generates_the_3d_finish` too. The new band tests in `crates/app/tests/shared_face_bodies_finish.rs` keep the same assert, because the split must not change an assert.\n\nThe same `verify` reply also has `\"held_by\":[\"S1\"]` and many `S1` warnings of this type:\n\n```\nshank/holder at move 181 collides with the part or an island\nshank/holder at move 1452 collides with the uncut stock\n```\n\nBand 1 (top) has 273 findings, band 5 has 2587. The post is held, so the output is not silent. But no test asserts on these collisions.\n\n## What to do\n\n1. Make the no-gouge assert real: delete `R1` from the job of the band tests (or generate it, if #1749 makes it generate), so that the stock sim runs. Then assert `gate.problems` has no `gouge` entry.\n2. Find out if the shank/holder collisions of `S1` on the as-imported sample are correct. If they are correct, pin them by name. If they are wrong, file a defect.\n\n## Done means\n\nThe band tests run the verify gate (`gate.skipped` is absent) and assert on its result.\n",
